(footprint "DPAK_T2Tab_FanCopper" (version 20211014) (generator pcbnew)
  (layer "F.Cu")
  (tedit 0)
  (descr "DPAK (TO-252, SOT428) triac with heat-sink copper on the tab net (T2/MT2 = pad 2) on both faces. Pads of DPAK_ST_T8_Tab (ST DS2114 Rev 15 p.9 Fig. 14: tab pad 6.7 x 6.7, lead pads 3.0 x 1.6 at pitch 4.572), a superset of the WeEn BTA208S-800B recommended footprint (Rev.02 2025-03-19 p.10-11: tab pad 5.9 x 5.75, lead pads 1.4 x 2.4, pitch 4.57); pinning WeEn p.2 Table 2: pad 1 = T1 (MT1), pad 2 = T2 (tab, middle lead cut), pad 3 = G. Heat sink: pad 2 copper 10.5 x 11.0 mm (1.16 cm2, tab included, solder mask over all but the tab pad) on F.Cu and the same on B.Cu, joined by 14 plated holes 0.3/0.6 mm outside the tab pad (no solder wicking under the tab); ST DS2114 Fig. 12 p.6 (DPAK on FR4 35 um): Rth(j-a) about 59 C/W at 1.16 cm2 under the tab (read between 60 at 1.0 and 52 at 2.0; B.Cu not credited). Size held by the mains isolation-band fill on the 40 x 76 board (sign-off-6 q1): 1760 of 2006 mm2, 88 %. The 14 holes are also the FAN layer change at the switch (14 parallel barrels; timed-bathroom-vent sign-off review S1/S2).")
  (tags "DPAK TO-252 SOT428 triac heatsink")
